05","b":"2TI","v":"anf.tertullian.de_carne_christi","w":"tertullian.de_carne_christi","a":"tertullian","s":17,"p":[0,0],"r":[4,14],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Although Tertullian dignifies him with an ille , we have no particulars of this man. [It may be that this is an epithet , rather than a name, given to some enemy of truth like Zlexander the \"Coppersmith\" (2 Tim. iv. 14) or like that (1 Tim. i. 20), blasphemer, whose character suits the case.]"},{"id":"2a6065792cfe","b":"1TI","v":"anf.tertullian.de_carne_christi","w":"tertullian.de_carne_christi","a":"tertullian","s":17,"p":[0,0],"r":[1,20],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Although Tertullian dignifies him with an ille , we have no particulars of this man. [It may be that this is an epithet , rather than a name, given to some enemy of truth like Zlexander the \"Coppersmith\" (2 Tim. iv. 14) or like that (1 Tim. i. 20), blasphemer, whose character suits the case.]"},{"id":"2bafcf7384dc","b":"ROM","v":"anf.tertullian.de_carne_christi","w":"tertullian.de_carne_christi","a":"tertullian","s":17,"p":[0,0],"r":[8,3],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"\"Tertullian, referring to St. Paul, says of Christ: `Evacuavit peccatum in carne; 0' alluding, as I suppose, to Romans viii. 3. But the corresponding Greek in the printed editions is κατέκρινε τὴν ἁμαρτίαν ἐν τῇ σαρκί (`He condemned sin in the flesh 0'). Had Tertullian a different reading in his Greek mss., or did he confound Romans viii. 3 with Romans vi. 6, i#na καταργηθῇ τὸ σῶμα τὴς ἁμαρτίας (`that the body of sin might be destroyed 0')? Jerome translates the Greek καταργέω by `evacuo, 0' c. xvi. See Adv. Marcionem , ver. 14. Dr. Neander has pointed out two passages in which Tertullian has `damnavit or damnaverit delinquentiam in carne. 0' See de Res. Carnis. 46; de Pudicitiâ. 17.\"-Bp. Kaye."},{"id":"57b6fa06885c","b":"ROM","v":"anf.tertullian.de_carne_christi","w":"tertullian.de_carne_christi","a":"tertullian","s":17,"p":[0,0],"r":[6,6],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"\"Tertullian, referring to St. Paul, says of Christ: `Evacuavit peccatum in carne; 0' alluding, as I suppose, to Romans viii. 3. But the corresponding Greek in the printed editions is κατέκρινε τὴν ἁμαρτίαν ἐν τῇ σαρκί (`He condemned sin in the flesh 0'). Had Tertullian a different reading in his Greek mss., or did he confound Romans viii. 3 with Romans vi. 6, i#na καταργηθῇ τὸ σῶμα τὴς ἁμαρτίας (`that the body of sin might be destroyed 0')? Jerome translates the Greek καταργέω by `evacuo, 0' c. xvi. See Adv. Marcionem , ver. 14. Dr. Neander has pointed out two passages in which Tertullian has `damnavit or damnaverit delinquentiam in carne. 0' See de Res. Carnis. 46; de Pudicitiâ. 17.\"-Bp. Kaye."},{"id":"c2bff79e6164","b":"ISA","v":"anf.tertullian.de_carne_christi","w":"tertullian.de_carne_christi","a":"tertullian","s":18,"p":[0,0],"r":[7,14],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Isa. vii. 14."},{"id":"53bed353cbbb","b":"MAT","v":"anf.tertullian.de_carne_christi","w":"tertullian.de_carne_christi","a":"tertullian","s":18,"p":[0,0],"r":[1,23],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Matt. i. 23."},{"id":"fb42a4565cad","b":"GEN","v":"anf.tertullian.de_carne_christi","w":"tertullian.de_carne_christi","a":"tertullian","s":18,"p":[0,0],"r":[2,7],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Gen. ii. 7."},{"id":"a0750b0efd6b","b":"MAT","v":"anf.tertullian.de_carne_christi","w":"tertullian.de_carne_christi","a":"tertullian","s":19,"p":[0,0],"r":[12,41],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Matt. xii. 41, 42."},{"id":"c8e8fda93a39","b":"JHN","v":"anf.tertullian.de_carne_christi","w":"tertullian.de_carne_christi","a":"tertullian","s":19,"p":[0,0],"r":[1,14],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"John i. 14."},{"id":"95ec525d5750","b":"JHN","v":"anf.tertullian.de_carne_christi","w":